    <h1 class="doc-h">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: October 2026</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p><b>The short version:</b> there are no accounts and no sign-in. Your
      teams and settings stay on your Mac. On iPhone and iPad, background alerts
      and pinned Live Activities use the delivery information described below.
      We also collect anonymous usage and crash data. We don't sell your data.</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Anonymous analytics</b>: which screens you open, which buttons
        you use, which settings you toggle, which teams get followed (by
        numeric team id), and whether alerts and goal confetti reached your
        screen - plus crash reports (via Firebase Analytics/Crashlytics) so we
        can keep the app working. It's tied to a random app-instance
        identifier, never to your name, email or any account.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name, email address, or any other personal details. The app
        has no accounts, so there is nothing to sign in with.</li>
        <li>Your Mac's saved team list and alert settings, or your device's theme
        preference. The Mac app does not register push subscriptions.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How the app gets scores</h2>
      <p>The app's match scores are plain files downloaded from our Cloudflare-hosted
      server, and team crests come from API-Sports' image server. Like any web
      request, these servers see your IP address in the course of sending the
      file; we don't log it against you or send anything about you with the
      request.</p>

      <h2>Optional iPhone and iPad background delivery</h2>
      <p>When background delivery is configured and you enable match notifications,
      the app sends its Apple notification token, selected numeric team IDs, and
      alert preferences to our push service. Pinning a match sends that match's
      numeric ID and Live Activity token. An opaque device-generated credential
      identifies this installation; we store only its hash. Firebase App Check
      verifies that registration requests come from our app. No account is needed.</p>
      <p>These subscriptions are stored in Google Cloud and used to send updates
      through Apple's Push Notification service. Turning off match notifications
      and removing all pins requests deletion of the subscription when the app
      can connect. Subscriptions expire after 30 days without a successful refresh;
      queued delivery records expire shortly after delivery or their retry window,
      with deletion scheduled within about a day. Infrastructure request logs may
      include IP addresses; application logs omit notification tokens and credentials.</p>

      <h2>Where it lives</h2>
      <p>Anonymous analytics and crash reports are processed by Google
      (Firebase). Optional mobile push subscriptions are processed in Google Cloud,
      and notification content is delivered through Apple. Other preferences stay
      on your device.</p>

      <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
      <p>Before removing the mobile app, turn off match notifications and remove
      all pins while connected to delete the active subscription. Uninstalling
      cannot itself contact our server; unrefreshed subscriptions expire as above.
      Analytics can't be
      linked back to you, so there is no profile for us to delete - but if you
      have a question, email
      <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>

      <h2>Website demo</h2>
      <p>The embedded demo is hosted by YouTube. When the player loads or you
      watch the video, your browser connects to YouTube, which handles playback
      under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p><a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a></p>
